  PASS  L1b with c added: an M-free group containing a0 exists (kappa itself)
  variables ['G', 'rho', 'M', 'a0', 'muK'] -> 2 dimensionless group(s)
    exponents {'G': '-1', 'rho': '-2/3', 'M': '-1/3', 'a0': '1', 'muK': '0'}
    exponents {'G': '0', 'rho': '-1/3', 'M': '1/3', 'a0': '0', 'muK': '1'}
  with the clock mass mu_K (a length^-1) instead of c: a0 mu_K/(G rho) is M-free; mu_K is bounded and free
